INT. TOWER OF THE LAST STAIR - NIGHT

A circular stone chamber at the top of a thousand steps. A cracked crystal on a pedestal pulses faintly. Rain lashes the narrow windows.

ALDRIC, 40s, a battered knight in dented plate, leans on his sword. THESSALY, 30s, a sorceress in midnight blue, traces runes in the dust with a fingertip. GORM, 50s, a heavy-set dwarf with a braided beard, sits on the top stair, catching his breath. MIRREN, 18, a thief in a patched green cloak, circles the pedestal and eyes the crystal.

ALDRIC
Thessaly, how long before the seal gives?

THESSALY
Before dawn, if I'm right. Before midnight, if I'm wrong.

GORM
What do you think the odds are, Mirren?

MIRREN
Don't ask me. I'm the one who stole the map.

ALDRIC
We've all stolen something, little one.

THESSALY
Mirren, step back from the crystal.

MIRREN
I'm only looking.

THESSALY
Looking is how it begins.

GORM
Thessaly's right. My grandfather looked at a gem like that once. Went blind in one eye. Then the other.

MIRREN
Gorm, your grandfather went blind from drinking.

GORM
That too.

ALDRIC
Enough. We climbed a thousand stairs for this. We say what we came to say.

THESSALY
What did we come to say, Aldric?

ALDRIC
That we will not let the King's witch-hunters have it.

GORM
We'd have been better off smashing it and going home.

THESSALY
Smash it and the city drowns.

MIRREN
You never told me that.

THESSALY
You never asked, Mirren.

ALDRIC
I did not tell either of you because I did not want you to leave.

GORM
(quietly)
Then you're a fool, knight. Or a liar.

ALDRIC
Perhaps both.

MIRREN
Then why are we fighting over it?

THESSALY
We're not.

GORM
Speak for yourself.

ALDRIC
Gorm. Put down your axe.

GORM
I didn't pick it up.

MIRREN
You did. It's in your hand.

Gorm looks down. The axe is there. His hand is trembling. The crystal pulses brighter.

THESSALY
It's speaking to you. To all of us. Close your ears.

GORM
I hear it. It says Aldric lied.

ALDRIC
Gorm--

The crystal flares. The windows blow in on a wave of white light.
